package environment

// AppInstructions is shared product policy, independent of a project's framework.
const AppInstructions = `Runtime contract for backend applications:
Service names must be unique lowercase identifiers (letters, digits, underscores; start with a letter; at most 32 characters). The name database is reserved; app is allowed only for the root route /.
Write ai-os.app.json at the workspace root using version 1, for example:
The manifest is strictly validated. Top-level fields are version, database, ai, build, services, and checks. Build and check steps accept command and optional cwd, not name or other metadata.
{"version":1,"database":"postgres","build":[{"cwd":"api","command":["go","build","-o","server","."]}],"services":[{"name":"api","cwd":"api","command":["./server"],"route":"/api","healthPath":"/api/health"},{"name":"web","cwd":"web","command":["node","server.js"],"route":"/","healthPath":"/"}],"checks":[{"command":["python3","tests/acceptance.py"]}]}
Use only the services and steps needed. Commands are argument arrays, not implicit shell strings. Cwd is workspace-relative. Supported toolchains are installed system binaries or project-local executables; never require host config or a Docker socket. One root route / is required. Route prefixes are preserved (/api/x reaches the API as /api/x). The host supplies HOST=127.0.0.1 and a distinct PORT to each service, NAME_URL for each service (except app), APP_URL for the route gateway, and DATABASE_URL when PostgreSQL is requested. Bind HOST and PORT; never hardcode ports or credentials. Serve a usable UI at the root service. Checks must use these URLs, exit nonzero on failure, test requested behavior and validation, and clean up only their own test records. Build steps run before services; checks run after every service is HTTP-ready. Readiness is not proof of correctness.
Declare database:postgres when a managed database is needed; the host provisions it on Build & start app. Preserve existing data with migrations. If no DATABASE_URL exists during coding, report integration checks as pending runtime verification; do not silently replace a requested managed database with a different store. Static HTML needs no runtime manifest. Report exactly what was tested, and tell the user to use Build & start app for backend applications. Do not claim a completed coding job is a deployed or verified application.
For requested text-AI features, declare "ai":"ollama". At runtime the host supplies OLLAMA_BASE_URL and OLLAMA_MODEL for the existing signed-in Ollama daemon and Gemma cloud model. Call POST /api/chat from the app backend, never the browser; use model from OLLAMA_MODEL, messages, and stream:false or handle the streaming protocol. Validate input size, bound requests, handle provider errors and cancellation, and show loading/error states. Keep readiness independent of model availability. Test with a stub by default; do not spend cloud quota in startup checks. Runtime AI usage is separate from build usage and consumes the operator's Ollama account quota. Gemma text generation is not image generation. Image, speech, payment, and other external services require a separately configured provider; report missing capabilities instead of inventing endpoints, credentials, or successful output.

`
